CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ one element: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ by value, two: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ static, two: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ class template, forwarding: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
typecheck_compound_declarator replicated the parameters (a$0, a$1) but not
the pack expansions of the trailing-return-type; those are now expanded,
and the replicated names, not yet declared there, become lvalue
placeholders of the parameters' types.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
